{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1119401-weapons-with-the-stun-quality-clarification","id":1119401,"title":"Weapons with the Stun Quality Clarification","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-22T21:30:04-07:00","id":1119401,"title":"Weapons with the Stun Quality Clarification","content":"In order to inflict the Stunned Tilt, one needs to deal as much damage as the target's size. Some weapons have the &quot;Stun&quot; Special, which &quot;Double the weapon bonus for purposes of the Stun Tilt&quot;.<br /> <br /> First off, I would like to point out that there is no &quot;Weapon Bonus&quot;, there is Damage, so that can be confusing. Second, what do they mean, &quot;Double the weapon bonus for purposes of the Stun Tilt&quot;? Take the Weapon Damage that the weapon normally does, multiply it by 2, and use that instead to compare it to the target's size? If I attack someone with a Sledgehammer (Damage+3) and get 2 successes, my attack is considered 8 for the purposes of inflicting the Stunned Tilt? So, if my target was Size 5 and had Armour 2, they would have the Stunned Tilt applied as for the purposes of receiving the Stunned Tilt, they received 6 damage, while only filling 3 wound boxes, whereas with a sword (+3), they would have not been Stunned as the damage would only have been 3 for the purposes of receiving the Stunned Tilt.<br /> <br /> Also, what's the point of giving the Stun Special to the Sap? It has a Damage of 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5387-peteman","name":"Peteman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}